## [ENT-015] | 2026-11-16 15:18 UTC | Unity | order | ref: governance/rulebook.md | see: ENT-014
Changed: on Suggi's word of 2026-11-16, about 14:50 to 15:00 UTC. The orders take a short form: his standing orders at the head, the plan in five steps (P1 to P5), then what every Admiral does and a short block for each. S6 is new in his words. The fleet's standing rules F1 to F21 moved into the rulebook, section 12, under their numbers and order nothing less; F8 (no ship is idle) and F19 (the measures) are new in his words. Each Admiral plans its own division; a session starts on one briefing; each member's own FLEET.md shows its ships' routes. The turn jobs are paused since 13:50 UTC on his word and start on his word.
In force from 2026-11-16 15:18 UTC until a newer entry.
STANDING ORDERS (Suggi; for the whole fleet; set and changed by him alone)
S1. Explore freely.
S2. Grow income; optimize the routes and the credits per hour.
S3. Evolve the fleet.
S4. Build bases and stations.
S5. Grow the fleet and the faction.
S6. Prepare all the material for one to two stations and learn how to build one; Suggi chooses the place later (Suggi, 2026-11-16: "prepare all the material for 1-2 stations and learn how to build it. I chose location in the future").
PLAN (the Fleet Admiral's reading of the standing orders, in five steps; Suggi and the Fleet Admiral change it together; strategy, phase 1: income)
P1. No ship is idle (S2, S3; Suggi, 2026-11-16: "The ships should never be idle ... as long as all ships are always leveling and doing stuff"). Every ship works all the time: it earns, or it levels and gathers. Rule F8.
  Goal: the fill gate says PASS for every role: 146 of 146 ships at work.
P2. Income that repeats, on routes that are never crowded (S2; Suggi: "never switch all the ships to the same routes"). A route gets no more ships than it carries: what its bid, its field or its herd regains per hour. A whole division on one buyer emptied every ice bid in half a day; the buyers are the limit, so new demand is the work: other goods, other stations, what we craft.
  Goal: steady income per hour above zero in every division, and rising.
P3. Level and upgrade (S3). A ship that earns nothing still levels; the next hull and fit are bought when wallet and skill allow (rule F17; Piloting 10, 20, 30 and 50 open hull tiers 2 to 5).
  Goal: every division names in its report what its pilots' levels gained and its next hull step.
P4. Gather and learn for the stations (S4, S6). One station takes a fee of 5,000,000 cr, one station core and the foundry that makes it (38,000,000 cr and about 30 raw inputs; the tool base_plan with kind=station prints each input, what we hold and what is missing). Standing work gathers the inputs into storage; Logistics keeps the list and tests the crafted steps by hand; Intel finds the sources the list lacks. Two stations take the list twice.
  Goal: per input the units held against the units needed, rising every turn; one recipe step tested per turn.
P5. One fleet (S5). The faction for every ship, with shared storage and shared money (rule F11), and the purse on the flagships (rule F20): the Fleet Admiral's steps, each on Suggi's word. More ships when a division shows work for more ships than it has (rule F5).
  Goal: Suggi has the live cost of each faction step before any is paid.
  The plan changes when Suggi and the Fleet Admiral change it.
TURN
T1. The first turn after this entry (Suggi, 2026-11-16): each Admiral checks its routes, names the standard routes its ships can always fly without running a bid, a field or a herd dry, and puts every ship of its division on work. The Fleet Admiral put four standing routes into the plans of Mining, Trade, Military and Intel at 15:10 UTC as a stopgap (gather-gsc-0027-prism-scatter and gather-hamal-crystal-bloom, 40 ships each; mine-acubens and mine-pherkad-rift, 18 ships each): each Admiral replaces them with standing work of its own choice, or keeps them and says why. At 15:16 UTC the fill gate read 145 of 146 ships at work.
  Done when: the fill gate says PASS for the role; the Standing Plan in the guidebook names each route with its ships and what it carries; FLEET.md carries the section Routes Now; the report gives the division's income per hour, its ships at work and its one-time money apart (rule F19).
EVERY ADMIRAL
