he file; your turn starts it and your next turn reads its record. A hand flight is the first try of a call only.
Measure: income per hour; reserve inputs stored per hour; drones at work, 50 of 50; ships lost, which stays 0; what the combat skills gained; pirates: where they stand and what they are, the test's result, and what a group against them takes.
ORACLE, Intel (the scout- ships)
Order: a scout scans all the time. Give every scout routes of its own, as templates of reads: the places our routes use are read twice in a turn, the order books the fleet sells to are read every hour, and a scout that ends one read starts the next, the oldest reading first; a scout gathers ore only when nothing the fleet plans on is stale. Keep about ten scouts exploring the galaxy and about twenty where the fleet works, as you decide (rule F26). The explorers read first every system on the roads to Yildun and to Aldebaran, then on to Hawthorne and Alchiba (scripts/map.py route nexus_prime <system>): each place, field, herd, station and order book, filed the same turn in the system's file; say in your report what each site and each system on the way holds. Find a source for each input of the reserve that has none: caustic sac (429 short for the offices) and silicon ore first. The three station sites you named stay on record beside the four Suggi named. Your turn of 18:23 UTC ended without a report on a fault of the tools, which is fixed: this turn also gives every scout routes of its own. Read where pirates stand in and around our space and on the roads to the sites (how many, what ships) and write it down for Military (observe.py add pirate <system id> ...): your scouts look and leave, they do not fight (rule F27).
Measure: the age of the oldest reading the fleet plans on, at the end of the turn; places our routes use that were read twice; inputs of the reserve with a known source; scouts at work, 30 of 30; what scanning, exploration and navigation gained; scouts exploring, about 10 of 30; systems read on the roads to the sites.


